c0bb928f57c6d252ddd506a3f","event_uuid":"fd208d68-ab75-4b78-8f23-231a96cd2274","position":{"commit_sha":"5749bb79e88fb2e4c3b3b9babeceee88d043e0f3","position":"1787389815869224001-fd208d68-ab75-4b78-8f23-231a96cd2274"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLOSE: close gate(s) bypassed by user approval — no completion/signature attestation was signed. Reason: \"Change 2091 MERGED with LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 (both Gerrit gates green). Stale-material is from post-review file_impact correction to the actual merged files (outbound_comments/differ/mutation_builders + test_parent_breadcrumb) and AC-tick description edit; no plan substance changed. Held-out oracle 8/8 green, teeth-verified.\". Session: a330d41420.","timestamp":1787389815869224001}],"created_at":1787290330607276001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5bc0b98f-a5fa-4c31-b452-9c4b48d9748e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a8ea-be28-2394-4f0c"},{"link_uuid":"ee6c4e9f-48af-4d97-8c9a-c8310c201c3b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ca67-c203-ee2c-4b03"},{"link_uuid":"7e4da513-c0bf-48c0-b8a4-ff5b156dfc4d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"72df-fc1e-a3e1-4aa4"}],"description":"# Parent-drift breadcrumb comment (echo-safe, nearest-represented-ancestor)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nWhen a local parent cannot be represented in Jira — the parent is a non-epic and this\nproject permits only Epic parents — the outbound differ already **suppresses the parent\nfield** before it is sent (`adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:196-215`: `parent_id in\nlocal_ticket_types` and `parent_type != \"epic\"` ⇒ the parent diff is dropped via\n`suppressed_out`/`dropped_field_sink`). The child then lands as an under-defined leaf with\nno hint that its defining context lives elsewhere. Alt-link self-heal was rejected as\necho-unsafe. We need an echo-safe breadcrumb comment pointing the Jira user at the nearest\nancestor that *is* visible in Jira, never re-ingested inbound.\n\n## Approach\n\nEmit the breadcrumb from the **outbound comment differ**, not the apply-time scalar\nrecorder `pass_io.record_parent_divergence` (see Scope for why that seam is wrong).\nIntegrate it into `outbound_comments._diff_comments` (`outbound_comments.py:385`), which\nalready (a) resolves the child's full Jira comment list `jira_comments` (from the\nsnapshot, or one bounded `client.get_comments` live fetch when the snapshot lacks the\n`comment` field — bug-4292 invariant), (b) builds the marker-stripped `jira_bodies` dedup\nset, (c) holds `binding_store` and the `TicketTransport` `client`. Reusing the resolved\n`jira_comments` avoids a second fetch.\n\nOn a bound child whose direct parent is type-collapsed (the suppression above), walk the\nchain upward and name the **nearest ancestor with a bound Jira key** (`binding_store.get_jira_key`). Build the body via `_decorate_outbound_comment`\n(`outbound_comments.py:209`, appends `RECONCILER_MARKER`) and return it as an ordinary\n`{\"action\":\"add\",...}` mutation appended to `_diff_comments`' result, posted through the\nexisting path (`dispatch_apply_phases._update_one_dispatch_comments:347` →\n`client.add_comment`, implemented by both backends: `adapters/jira/backend.py:361`,\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:558`).\n\n**Echo-safety (corrected).** The breadcrumb *is* mirrored outbound, so it must NOT be\ncaught by `_is_machine_marker_comment` (`outbound_comments.py:375-382`) — that matches\nonly `_EXCLUDED_COMMENT_PREFIXES` (`'BRIDGE_CANARY_ALERT:'`, `'Still stale as of'`) and\nwould *exclude* a comment from being sent; the body starts with neither prefix. Inbound\necho-safety comes solely from the `RECONCILER_MARKER` substring check in\n`inbound_collection_diffs._diff_comments_inbound` (`inbound_collection_diffs.py:154`: `if\nRECONCILER_MARKER in body_text: continue`). `_normalize_comment_body`\n(`outbound_comments.py:184-206`) **strips** `RECONCILER_MARKER`, so the marker never makes\n`_is_machine_marker_comment` fire and never enters the dedup key — it serves only the\ninbound suppression at line 154.**Append-once / supersede.** Dedup on a **stable identity tag**\n(`<!-- rebar:parent-breadcrumb -->`), not the variable ancestor key: before appending,\nscan the resolved `jira_comments` (normalized via `_normalize_comment_body`, which does\nnot strip this tag) for the tag; if present, emit nothing. This is append-once and stable\nacross passes — if the nearest represented ancestor later changes, a breadcrumb is still detected so no conflicting second one is appended (first-writer-wins). The\noutbound comment path is ADD-only (no transport-portable edit/delete), so the original is\nintentionally not rewritten (accepted limitation below). Adds no transport capability,\ncannot loop.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `outbound_comments.py` — add pure `_build_parent_breadcrumb(...)` and integrate it into\n  `_diff_comments` (`:385`): after `jira_bodies` is built, when the drift condition holds\n  and no resolved comment carries the tag, append one decorated `\"add\"`. New\n  `_diff_comments` params `local_parents` (`{id->parent_id}`) and `local_ticket_types`,\n  both defaulting to `None` (no breadcrumb when absent — every existing caller/test\n  unchanged).\n- `outbound_mutation_builders.py` — in `_compute_outbound_update_mutation` (`:163`), pass\n  the new `local_parents` (threaded from the caller) and the already-in-scope\n  `local_ticket_types` into the `_diff_comments(...)` call (`:277`).\n- `outbound_differ.py` — in `compute_outbound_mutations` (`:449`), build `local_parents`\n  `{t[\"ticket_id\"]: t.get(\"parent_id\")}` beside the existing `local_ticket_types` build\n  (`:551`) and thread it into `_compute_outbound_update_mutation`.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_parent_breadcrumb.py` (new).\n\n**Out of scope (with reason):** `pass_io.record_parent_divergence` (`pass_io.py:80`) and\nits call sites `dispatch_one.py:558,569,579` and `acli_cli_ops.py:158` are NOT touched.\nIts signature `(kind, key, local_id, parent, exc, repo_root)` is scalar-only — `parent`\nis the *failed* key/CLEAR sentinel — with no ticket graph, binding store, comment client,\nor snapshot; `acli_cli_ops.py:158` passes `local_id=None` (transport boundary), so it\nstructurally cannot supply the inputs. The differ seam detects the same drift class\nearlier with all inputs present.\n\n**UPDATE path only.** The breadcrumb needs the child's Jira issue to exist (to post +\ndedupe), so it is emitted from the bound path; on the create pass the parent is dropped\nat birth but there is no child key yet, and the breadcrumb follows next pass. CREATE is\nuntouched.\n\n## Body content contract\n\nDeterministic (no timestamps, so dedup is stable). Nearest ancestor `PROJ-42`:\n\n```\nThis ticket's parent hierarchy could not be fully represented in Jira. Nearest tracked ancestor: PROJ-42. Full parent context is maintained in rebar.\n<!-- rebar:parent-breadcrumb -->\n\n<!-- rebar:reconciler-echo -->\n```\n\nIf ≥1 intervening ancestor was skipped for lacking a bound key, insert `One or more\nintervening parent levels are not represented in Jira.` before the last sentence. The\nfirst line starts with no `_EXCLUDED_COMMENT_PREFIXES` value (mirrored outbound); the\ntrailing `RECONCILER_MARKER` guarantees inbound suppression.\n\n## Accepted limitation\n\nNo supersede/edit of a stale breadcrumb: the path is ADD-only and no transport-portable\nedit/delete exists, so a changed nearest ancestor leaves the original in place — still a\nvalid \"context lives upward, see rebar\" pointer, preferred over conflicting duplicates.\n\n## Portability\n\nIn-process differ logic plus the existing `TicketTransport` comment port (`add_comment`/\n`get_comments`), implemented by both backends. No CI-system dependency, no new binary,\nfilesystem assumption, or transport capability; runs identically across library/CLI/MCP\nand both Jira deployments. With `local_parents`/`local_ticket_types` absent it is a no-op.\n\n## Testing\n\nIn-process unit tests over `_build_parent_breadcrumb`/`_diff_comments` (stub binding store,\nsynthetic snapshots; pure logic).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A bound child with a type-collapsed, bound parent appends exactly one breadcrumb\n  naming the nearest represented ancestor's Jira key and carrying both the\n  `<!-- rebar:parent-breadcrumb -->` tag and `RECONCILER_MARKER` — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_emitted`.\n- [x] Append-once via the stable tag, including when the nearest represented ancestor\n  changes across passes (no conflicting second comment) — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_idempotent_across_ancestor_change`.\n- [x] When the walk skips an unbound intervening ancestor to reach a bound one, the body\n  names the bound ancestor and states the intervening levels are not represented —\n  verified by `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_unrepresented_intervening_ancestor_noted`.\n- [x] No ancestor with a bound Jira key ⇒ no breadcrumb — verified by\n  `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_omitted_when_no_bound_ancestor`.\n- [x] The breadcrumb body is suppressed inbound by `_diff_comments_inbound` (carries\n  `RECONCILER_MARKER`) — verified by `test_parent_breadcrumb.py::test_breadcrumb_echo_safe`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py","reason":"parent-drift breadcrumb builder + _diff_comments params"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"thread local_parents/local_ticket_types"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py","reason":"build local_parents map, thread to differ"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_parent_breadcrumb.py","reason":"held-out breadcrumb oracle (8 tests)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","force_close_reason":"Change 2091 MERGED with LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 (both Gerrit gates green). Stale-material is from post-review file_impact correction to the actual merged files (outbound_comments/differ/mutation_builders + test_parent_breadcrumb) and AC-tick description edit; no plan substance changed. Held-out oracle 8/8 green, teeth-verified.","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","a8ea-be28-2394-4f0c"],["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"],["relates_to","72df-fc1e-a3e1-4aa4"],["relates_to","ca67-c203-ee2c-4b03"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"dfce743a-829f-493e-a63c-7c8134afebd7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2c66-205d-92e1-4419","ticket_type":"story","title":"Parent-drift breadcrumb comment (echo-safe, nearest-represented-ancestor)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a3ad8051-a133-4ab1-9d3b-8f50fa988f51","dfd38142-c403-44e5-a713-f05ecc985066","e71501ab-0bd2-4175-9856-4fbc32d547fa","138bcb7c-e42b-49da-8d00-9839ffa072bb","cd3545c8-46dd-4761-bb32-cdaa8bdd2481","1d6f59d3-be77-4e33-8784-6f8f28604c1c","ee6c4e9f-48af-4d97-8c9a-c8310c201c3b","ffb46a99-bd3a-4ab3-9ed1-881b331df3a6","7e4da513-c0bf-48c0-b8a4-ff5b156dfc4d","9f8c22ca-aaf4-4773-a59c-5a3b8c8b7a0f","a6b4e165-390b-4c14-87d2-112006c7ef59","dfce743a-829f-493e-a63c-7c8134afebd7","fd208d68-ab75-4b78-8f23-231a96cd2274"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":17